# SleepFactor: Testing, Version Control, and Release

This document consolidates **development testing**, **Git/version workflow**, **Android production (GitHub Actions)**, **iOS production (EAS + TestFlight)**, and **marketing website** checks. Older **`testing.mdc`** content lives here; **`testing.mdc`** now defers to this file.

**Related rules:** **`Learnings.mdc`** (debugging and past native fixes), **`versioning.mdc`** (automatic version bumps on merge), **`IOS-Android-testing.mdc`** (call out when a change is platform-specific).

---

## App identities & EAS profiles

| Variant | Purpose | Bundle / package | How testers get it |
|--------|---------|------------------|-------------------|
| **SleepFactor Dev** | Fast iteration with Metro | `com.sleepfactor.app.dev` | EAS **development** profile (dev client); `npx expo start --dev-client` (+ tunnel or LAN) |
| **SleepFactor** (Android prod) | Store-style release binary | `com.sleepfactor.app` | GitHub Releases **APK** after merge to `main` (automated workflow) |
| **SleepFactor** (iOS prod) | TestFlight / App Store | `com.sleepfactor.app` | EAS **production** iOS build → **submit** to App Store Connect → **TestFlight** (and later App Store) |

**`eas.json`** sets **`APP_VARIANT`** to **`development`** or **`production`** per build profile so **`app.config.js`** resolves the correct bundle ID and display name (**SleepFactor Dev** vs **SleepFactor**). **`appVersionSource`** is **local** (versions follow **`package.json`** / app config).

---

## End-to-end workflow (high level)

1. **Develop & test** — feature branch, **SleepFactor Dev**, dev server (**tunnel** preferred; **LAN** if tunnel/ngrok fails). **Android first** when possible; **also validate on iPhone** after native, HealthKit, or iOS-facing changes.
2. **Review** — PR, checks, merge to **`main`** when approved.
3. **Ship Android prod** — GitHub Actions builds production **APK**, bumps version (+0.0.1 pattern per **`versioning.mdc`** / workflow), GitHub Release.
4. **Ship iOS beta/prod binary** — separate step: **EAS production iOS build** + **`eas submit`** → TestFlight (and App Store when ready). *Not* triggered automatically by the same merge unless you add or run that pipeline.

---

## Staged checklist: backend + app + iOS TestFlight (reference)

Use this when a release touches **Supabase** and/or needs a **new production iOS binary** (not only Metro reload).

| Stage | What to do |
|-------|------------|
| **1. Dev testing** | Feature branch; **`npx expo start --dev-client`** (tunnel or LAN); test on **SleepFactor Dev**; shake → **Reload** to pick up JS. Rebuild the **dev client** only if native deps, permissions, or native app config changed (**see Phase 1**). |
| **2. Production database** | Apply pending **Supabase migrations** to the **production** project the **production** app uses (CLI **`npx supabase db push`** when linked to prod, or **SQL Editor** in the dashboard). Schema must match the app **before** or **with** the store/TestFlight binary, or users can see errors. Example: migrations under **`supabase/migrations/`** (e.g. global consumption presets). |
| **3. Commit** | Commit (or merge) the exact code you intend to ship so the EAS build is reproducible. |
| **4. Version & iOS build number** | Bump **`package.json`** **`version`** when you want a new user-facing / runtime version. For **every** new upload to App Store Connect, increment **`ios.buildNumber`** in **`app.config.js`** (Apple rejects duplicate **CFBundleVersion** values). This repo sets it explicitly on the **`ios`** object (e.g. **`buildNumber: "1328"`** — increment the string for each new TestFlight/App Store upload). |
| **5. EAS production iOS build** | **`eas build --platform ios --profile production`** (or **`npx eas-cli build …`**). Uses **`eas.json`** profile **`production`** (**`APP_VARIANT: production`**, **`com.sleepfactor.app`**). |
| **6. Submit to Apple** | **`eas submit --platform ios --latest`** (or submit from the Expo dashboard). |
| **7. TestFlight** | Wait for **processing** in App Store Connect; assign the build to **internal** / **external** groups; testers update via the **TestFlight** app. |

**Android production APK** (GitHub Actions after merge to **`main`**) is a separate path; see **Phase 3a**.

**Expo Updates / OTA:** JS-only fixes *may* ship via **EAS Update** if configured; **native** or **config-plugin** changes need a **new `eas build`**. When unsure, ship a new production binary.

